<title>FRANCE: Bosch's voting rights in Valeo up.</title>
<headline>Bosch's voting rights in Valeo up.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>French car parts company Valeo said on Monday that Robert Bosch GmbH's voting rights in the group had risen to 9.36 percent from 4.96 percent as the result of an automatic doubling of voting rights after four years of Valeo share ownership.</p>
<p>It said privately owned components group Robert Bosch GmbH has been a shareholder in Valeo since 1978.</p>
<p>Since 1987, it has reduced its holding in Valeo's capital from 7.3 percent to 5.1 percent currently, Valeo said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
